cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata below, together with the WDM papers listed under references."
title: "wdm_models_scripts: code release for the WDM time-frequency transform papers I and II"
abstract: >-
  Code release accompanying "The WDM Time-Frequency Transform in Gravitational-Wave
  Data Analysis" Papers I (Formalism) and II (evolutionary spectra). It contains three
  Python packages: wdm (distribution wdm-paper; the WDM transforms, Paper I algorithms
  and stateless Paper II kernels), domainia (time, frequency and WDM data vectors,
  covariance operators and likelihoods; dual NumPy/JAX) and wdm_models (the sinusoid
  and galactic-binary toy models), together with the scripts, shipped input data and
  golden reference values that reproduce the papers' toy-model results.
type: software
version: 0.9.0
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/AaronDJohnson/wdm_models_scripts"
